      "source": "tianxia.subpath.body.heaven_answering_adaptive_body.feature.meridians_remember_affliction",
      "name": "Meridians Remember Affliction",
      "text": "CL6 - Meridians Remember Affliction\nOnce per round after failing a save and becoming Blinded, Charmed, Frightened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, Restrained, or Stunned, record it as your Affliction Adaptation until scene end. Maintain one.\nWhile affected by the adapted condition:\n- Add Proficiency Bonus to saves made to end it.\n- If no save is normally allowed during your turn, spend 2 Stamina at the end of your turn to repeat the original save against the original DC, once per round.\nNormalized Procedure — Meridians Remember Affliction\n- Gain an Affliction Adaptation only after failing a hostile save and actually becoming one of the listed conditions. Several eligible conditions from one failed save create one chosen Adaptation.\n- Acquisition occurs once per round. At the current one-record limit, a new record can replace the existing one or be declined.\n- Add Proficiency Bonus to every save made specifically to end the adapted condition, including repeat saves printed by its source. This bonus does not apply to the initial save that created the Adaptation.\n- When the condition normally grants no save during your turn, at the end of your turn you may spend 2 Stamina to repeat the original save using the original ability and DC. This can occur once per round.\n- A successful repeat ends only the adapted condition and failure-only ongoing functions directly dependent on it. It does not reverse damage, movement, consumed resources, a completed transformation, or another condition unless its Source Rule links them.\n- If the original source no longer exists, use its recorded DC. If no valid original DC was recorded, use the fallback Authority DC for its Realm."
