      "text": "CL3 - Four-Hand Sequence\nOnce per turn when you take the Attack action, spend 1 Battle Hand to choose one:\n- Draw or stow two weapons.\n- Move 5 feet without provoking.\n- Gain +1 AC until your next turn.\n- After one attack misses, add Proficiency Bonus to the attack roll, potentially turning it into a hit.\n- After one attack hits, deal additional damage equal to Proficiency Bonus.\nOnly one Battle Hand can modify the same attack roll.\nNormalized Procedure — Four-Hand Sequence\n- Once during each of your turns when you take the Attack action, spend 1 Battle Hand and choose one printed operation. The operation can occur at a legal point during that Attack action unless its trigger specifies a hit or miss.\n- Drawing or stowing two weapons changes only those two item states and does not grant another object interaction.\n- The 5-foot movement follows a legal route and does not provoke Opportunity Attacks.\n- The +1 AC begins when chosen and lasts until the start of your next turn. Reapplication refreshes and does not stack with itself.\n- After an attack roll misses, but before resolving any miss consequence, spend the Hand to add Proficiency Bonus to that roll. Recalculate the outcome against the same target and defenses. This can turn the miss into a hit but is not a reroll.\n- After an attack hits, add Proficiency Bonus as one damage type dealt by that attack to the triggering packet. It cannot critically multiply separately.\n- Only one Battle Hand operation can modify the same attack roll. A later operation that does not modify the roll, such as movement or AC, still cannot be selected because Four-Hand Sequence is once per turn."
