      "name": "Bitter Heartfire",
      "text": "3. Foundation Resource\nBitter Heartfire\nResource Rule: Effect\nMaximum: 1\nStarting Amount: 0\nHow You Gain It: After you miss a hostile creature with an attack or Foundation-aligned technique, after a hostile creature succeeds on a saving throw against your Foundation-aligned technique, or after you fail a saving throw or ability check against a hostile effect and remain conscious.\nGeneration Timing: After the qualifying trigger resolves\nGeneration Limit: Once per round\nExpiration: End of your next turn\nSame-Event Rule: Cannot be spent on the event that generated it.\nAnti-Farming and Counterplay: Avoid giving clean hostile failure, pressure with attrition, or tempt self-sabotage that does not generate Heartfire.\nFeatures That Spend It: Bitter Return Strike, Refuse the Bitter Lesson, Heartfire Surge, Refined: Nine Coals Remember, Refined: Pain Becomes Method\nGenerate Bitter Heartfire\nType: No Action / Triggered\nYou can use this when After you miss a hostile creature with an attack or Foundation-aligned technique, after a hostile creature succeeds on a saving throw against your Foundation-aligned technique, or after you fail a saving throw or ability check against a hostile effect and remain conscious.\nRange: Self\nTarget: Self\n Gain 1 Bitter Heartfire after the qualifying trigger resolves. Maximum 1. Once per round. It expires at the end of your next turn. You cannot spend Bitter Heartfire on the same event that generated it. You cannot generate it from voluntary failure, friendly or training effects, deliberately impossible rolls, intentionally chosen Disadvantage, harmless repeated obstacles, self-created danger, or self-sabotage.\nLimit: Maximum 1; once per round; expires end of next turn; no same-event spending; anti-farming burden applies.\nCounterplay and Boundaries: Avoid giving clean hostile failure, pressure with attrition, or tempt self-sabotage that does not generate Heartfire.\n\nPrinted spending examples (require the named feature):\n\nHeartfire Surge\nType: Bonus Action\nYou can use this when On your turn while you have Bitter Heartfire.\nCost: 1 Bitter Heartfire\nRange: Self\nTarget: Self\n Spend 1 Bitter Heartfire as a Bonus Action. You gain temporary Hit Points equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus + your Path key ability modifier. Before the end of this turn, the next attack roll you make against a hostile creature or the next eligible saving throw/check you make against hostile pressure has Advantage.\nLimit: Self only; temporary HP does not stack with itself; one Advantage window.\nCounterplay and Boundaries: Force the surge early, deny targets, or impose conditions that block attacks/actions.\n\nRefuse the Bitter Lesson\nType: Reaction\nYou can use this when You fail a saving throw or ability check against a hostile fear, despair, control, curse, heart-demon, poison, pain, or pressure effect.\nCost: 1 Bitter Heartfire\nRange: Self\nTarget: Self\n Spend 1 Bitter Heartfire as a Reaction. Add your Proficiency Bonus + your Path key ability modifier to the failed saving throw or ability check. If this changes the outcome, you succeed. If it does not change the outcome and the triggering effect deals damage, reduce that damage by your Proficiency Bonus. This is a hard-won correction, not a free reroll.\nLimit: Requires Reaction; self only; cannot spend on the same event that generated Bitter Heartfire.\nCounterplay and Boundaries: Bait the Reaction, use effects outside the scope, or pressure allies instead."
